@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il-interpretation-time`
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g6-nouns`
IMPORT `g6-notice-and-hearing`
IMPORT `g6-appeal-and-publication`

-- g6-tests-appeal-and-publication.l4: tests of ss.55-57.
-- Expected values were decided from the Hebrew of ss.55-57 (law.wiki lines 412-432; gazette pp. 196-197) and
-- from Interpretation Law s.10 before any run.  The dates:
--   s.56(a), notice of the decision delivered Wednesday 2 June 2027: 45 days from it, IL s.10(a), end on Saturday
--     17 July 2027 (3 to 30 June are 28 days, 1 to 17 July 17 more); if Friday 16 and Saturday 17 July are days of
--     rest (IL s.10(c), kind W) the end moves to Sunday 18 July 2027, 46 days after delivery;
--   a violator who made no representations (notice of intention delivered Wednesday 3 March 2027, treated as a
--     demand delivered Friday 2 April 2027): 45 days from 2 April end on Monday 17 May 2027; from the notice of
--     intention's own day, 45 days end on Saturday 17 April 2027;
--   s.57(e), a corporation's publication of 1 September 2027 lasts four years, to 1 September 2031; an
--     individual's two, to 1 September 2029; for a publication on 29 February 2028 an individual's two years end on
--     28 February 2030 (the month lacks the day) and a corporation's four on 29 February 2032 (a leap year).

§ `Tests of ss 55 to 57`

§§ `Fixtures`

`no day of rest at all` MEANS `Calendar of rest days` WITH `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS EMPTY
`Friday 16 and Saturday 17 July 2027 as days of rest` MEANS `Calendar of rest days` WITH `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS LIST (YMD 2027 7 16), (YMD 2027 7 17)
`Monday 3 September 2029 as a holiday` MEANS `Calendar of rest days` WITH `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS LIST (YMD 2029 9 3)
`Friday 2 and Saturday 3 April 2027 as days of rest` MEANS `Calendar of rest days` WITH `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS LIST (YMD 2027 4 2), (YMD 2027 4 3)

`an individual violator` MEANS Person WITH `reference for the person` IS "P-IND", `kind of person` IS `an individual`

`violation (1)` MEANS `work with no licence at all`
`violation (2)` MEANS `work without a licence of the kind appropriate to the system`

GIVEN item IS A `Listed violation`
      act IS A STRING
GIVETH A Violation
`a violation of` item `in the act` act MEANS
    Violation WITH `the violator` IS `an individual violator`
                 , `the listed violation` IS item
                 , `reference for the act` IS act
                 , `date of the act` IS YMD 2027 3 1

-- Positional fields of `Notice of intention`: delivered on, in writing, act+date, amount, period (days), right, deemed
-- demand, power to add, intention to publish name.
`a complete notice of intention delivered on 3 March 2027` MEANS `Notice of intention` OF YMD 2027 3 3, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, JUST 30, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
`a notice of intention that announces publication of the name` MEANS `Notice of intention` OF YMD 2027 3 3, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, JUST 30, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE

§§ `s 55: no more than one financial sanction for one act`

-- Two breaches of one act (items (1) and (2) of one act, "act-1"); a different act ("act-2").
#ASSERT     `s 55 — a financial sanction may still be imposed for` (`a violation of` `violation (1)` `in the act` "act-1") `given` EMPTY `and` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 55 — a financial sanction may still be imposed for` (`a violation of` `violation (2)` `in the act` "act-1") `given` (LIST (`a violation of` `violation (1)` `in the act` "act-1")) `and` FALSE
#ASSERT     `s 55 — a financial sanction may still be imposed for` (`a violation of` `violation (2)` `in the act` "act-2") `given` (LIST (`a violation of` `violation (1)` `in the act` "act-1")) `and` FALSE
-- A sanction under another law for the same act bars one under this Law.
#ASSERT NOT `s 55 — a financial sanction may still be imposed for` (`a violation of` `violation (1)` `in the act` "act-1") `given` EMPTY `and` TRUE

#ASSERT     `s 55 — no act has more than one financial sanction among` EMPTY
#ASSERT     `s 55 — no act has more than one financial sanction among` (LIST (`a violation of` `violation (1)` `in the act` "act-1"), (`a violation of` `violation (2)` `in the act` "act-2"))
#ASSERT NOT `s 55 — no act has more than one financial sanction among` (LIST (`a violation of` `violation (1)` `in the act` "act-1"), (`a violation of` `violation (2)` `in the act` "act-1"))

#TRACE `s 55 — the Commissioner shall not impose a further sanction for the same act` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `impose a further financial sanction for the same act` `the Commissioner` AT 3
#TRACE `s 55 — the Commissioner shall not impose a further sanction for the same act` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 3)

§§ `s 56(a): 45 days from the day notice of the decision was delivered, IL s.10(a) and IL s.10(c) (kind W)`

#ASSERT `s 56(a) — the last day of the 45 days from` (YMD 2027 6 2) `with` `no day of rest at all` EQUALS YMD 2027 7 17
#ASSERT `s 56(a) — the last day of the 45 days from` (YMD 2027 6 2) `with` `Friday 16 and Saturday 17 July 2027 as days of rest` EQUALS YMD 2027 7 18
#ASSERT `s 56(a) — without s 10(c), the last day of the 45 days from` (YMD 2027 6 2) EQUALS YMD 2027 7 17
#ASSERT `s 56(a) — the days from` (YMD 2027 6 2) `to the last day to appeal, with` `no day of rest at all` EQUALS 45
#ASSERT `s 56(a) — the days from` (YMD 2027 6 2) `to the last day to appeal, with` `Friday 16 and Saturday 17 July 2027 as days of rest` EQUALS 46

-- Both edges (fork F-ACTDAY).  An appeal filed ON the day notice of the decision is delivered is "within 45 days" of it; a
-- day before is not; the last day is inside; with 16 and 17 July as days of rest, 18 July is inside and 19 July is not.
#ASSERT NOT `s 56(a) — the day` (YMD 2027 6 1) `is within the period to appeal that runs from` (YMD 2027 6 2) `with` `no day of rest at all`
#ASSERT     `s 56(a) — the day` (YMD 2027 6 2) `is within the period to appeal that runs from` (YMD 2027 6 2) `with` `no day of rest at all`
-- The strict reading, callable: the period starts the day AFTER delivery.
#ASSERT NOT `s 56(a) — counting the day after delivery as the first day, the day` (YMD 2027 6 2) `is within the period to appeal that runs from` (YMD 2027 6 2) `with` `no day of rest at all`
#ASSERT     `s 56(a) — counting the day after delivery as the first day, the day` (YMD 2027 6 3) `is within the period to appeal that runs from` (YMD 2027 6 2) `with` `no day of rest at all`
#ASSERT     `s 56(a) — counting the day after delivery as the first day, the day` (YMD 2027 7 17) `is within the period to appeal that runs from` (YMD 2027 6 2) `with` `no day of rest at all`
#ASSERT NOT `s 56(a) — counting the day after delivery as the first day, the day` (YMD 2027 7 18) `is within the period to appeal that runs from` (YMD 2027 6 2) `with` `no day of rest at all`
#ASSERT     `s 56(a) — the day` (YMD 2027 6 3) `is within the period to appeal that runs from` (YMD 2027 6 2) `with` `no day of rest at all`
#ASSERT     `s 56(a) — the day` (YMD 2027 7 17) `is within the period to appeal that runs from` (YMD 2027 6 2) `with` `no day of rest at all`
#ASSERT NOT `s 56(a) — the day` (YMD 2027 7 18) `is within the period to appeal that runs from` (YMD 2027 6 2) `with` `no day of rest at all`
#ASSERT     `s 56(a) — the day` (YMD 2027 7 18) `is within the period to appeal that runs from` (YMD 2027 6 2) `with` `Friday 16 and Saturday 17 July 2027 as days of rest`
#ASSERT NOT `s 56(a) — the day` (YMD 2027 7 19) `is within the period to appeal that runs from` (YMD 2027 6 2) `with` `Friday 16 and Saturday 17 July 2027 as days of rest`

-- A violator who made no representations (F-APPEAL-DEEMED): the day the notice of the decision counts as delivered.
#ASSERT `s 56(a) — the day notice of the decision counts as delivered to a violator who made no representations` `a complete notice of intention delivered on 3 March 2027` NOTHING `no day of rest at all` EQUALS YMD 2027 4 2
#ASSERT `s 56(a) — the day notice of the decision counts as delivered to a violator who made no representations, taking the day the notice of intention was delivered` `a complete notice of intention delivered on 3 March 2027` EQUALS YMD 2027 3 3
#ASSERT `s 56(a) — the last day of the 45 days from` (YMD 2027 4 2) `with` `no day of rest at all` EQUALS YMD 2027 5 17
#ASSERT `s 56(a) — the last day of the 45 days from` (YMD 2027 3 3) `with` `no day of rest at all` EQUALS YMD 2027 4 17

-- The right: a MAY, only against a final decision of the Commissioner, lodged in the Magistrates' Court where the President sits.
#TRACE `s 56(a) — the violator may appeal to the Magistrates' Court` TRUE (YMD 2027 6 2) `no day of rest at all` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the violator` DOES `appeal a final decision of the Commissioner to the Magistrates' Court` `the violator` TRUE AT 45
#TRACE `s 56(a) — the violator may appeal to the Magistrates' Court` TRUE (YMD 2027 6 2) `no day of rest at all` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the violator` DOES `appeal a final decision of the Commissioner to the Magistrates' Court` `the violator` FALSE AT 10
#TRACE `s 56(a) — the violator may appeal to the Magistrates' Court` FALSE (YMD 2027 6 2) `no day of rest at all` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 10)

§§ `s 56(b): the appeal does not stay execution unless the Commissioner agreed or the court ordered`

#ASSERT NOT `s 56(b) — the filing of the appeal stays the execution of the decision, given` FALSE `and` FALSE
#ASSERT     `s 56(b) — the filing of the appeal stays the execution of the decision, given` TRUE `and` FALSE
#ASSERT     `s 56(b) — the filing of the appeal stays the execution of the decision, given` FALSE `and` TRUE
#ASSERT     `s 56(b) — the filing of the appeal stays the execution of the decision, given` TRUE `and` TRUE

§§ `s 56(c): refund of the amount paid, or the part reduced, with shekel interest (not the arrears fees of s.49, trap T40)`

-- The court ordered the return of the whole amount paid: 20,000.  It reduced the sanction to 15,000: 5,000 comes back.
#ASSERT `s 56(c) — the amount to be returned of` 20_000 `when the court reduced the sanction to` NOTHING EQUALS 20_000
#ASSERT `s 56(c) — the amount to be returned of` 20_000 `when the court reduced the sanction to` (JUST 15_000) EQUALS 5_000
#ASSERT `s 56(c) — the amount to be returned of` 20_000 `when the court reduced the sanction to` (JUST 20_000) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 56(c) — the amount to be returned of` 20_000 `when the court reduced the sanction to` (JUST 0) EQUALS 20_000
-- With the shekel interest the caller computes (100): 5,100.  Without it, the Law does not answer.
#ASSERT `s 56(c) — the amount returned with shekel interest` 5_000 `and` (JUST 100) EQUALS 5_100
#ASSERT `s 56(c) — the amount returned with shekel interest` 20_000 `and` (JUST 0) EQUALS 20_000
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 56(c) — the amount returned with shekel interest` 5_000 `and` NOTHING BECAUSE "s 56(c) — the shekel interest is fixed by the Interest and Linkage Law, whose rates are not in the sources, and none was supplied"
-- The stretch the interest runs over: from the day of payment to the day of return.
#ASSERT `s 56(c) — the days from` (YMD 2027 8 1) `until` (YMD 2028 2 1) EQUALS 184
#ASSERT `s 56(c) — the days from` (YMD 2027 8 1) `until` (YMD 2027 8 1) EQUALS 0

§§ `s 57(a): which of the six items the Law requires`

#ASSERT `s 57(a) — the numbers of the items the Law requires where` FALSE `and the violator is` `an individual` EQUALS LIST 1, 2, 3, 5
#ASSERT `s 57(a) — the numbers of the items the Law requires where` TRUE `and the violator is` `an individual` EQUALS LIST 1, 2, 3, 4, 5
#ASSERT `s 57(a) — the numbers of the items the Law requires where` FALSE `and the violator is` `a corporation` EQUALS LIST 1, 2, 3, 5, 6
#ASSERT `s 57(a) — the numbers of the items the Law requires where` TRUE `and the violator is` `a corporation` EQUALS LIST 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6

-- Positional fields of `Item of a publication under section 57(a)`: item number, published, barred (9(a)), omitted (9(b)).
`item (1) published`          MEANS `Item of a publication under section 57(a)` OF 1, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE
`item (2) published`          MEANS `Item of a publication under section 57(a)` OF 2, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE
`item (3) published`          MEANS `Item of a publication under section 57(a)` OF 3, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE
`item (4) published`          MEANS `Item of a publication under section 57(a)` OF 4, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE
`item (5) published`          MEANS `Item of a publication under section 57(a)` OF 5, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE
`item (6) published`          MEANS `Item of a publication under section 57(a)` OF 6, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE
`item (2) left out`           MEANS `Item of a publication under section 57(a)` OF 2, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`item (2) left out as s 9(b) allows` MEANS `Item of a publication under section 57(a)` OF 2, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`item (5) barred and not published`  MEANS `Item of a publication under section 57(a)` OF 5, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE
`item (5) barred but published`      MEANS `Item of a publication under section 57(a)` OF 5, TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE
`item (6) not required, not published` MEANS `Item of a publication under section 57(a)` OF 6, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

#ASSERT     `s 57(a), (d) — the item is dealt with as the Law requires` `item (2) published` `where it is required:` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 57(a), (d) — the item is dealt with as the Law requires` `item (2) left out` `where it is required:` TRUE
#ASSERT     `s 57(a), (d) — the item is dealt with as the Law requires` `item (2) left out as s 9(b) allows` `where it is required:` TRUE
-- s.9(a) bars it: it must not be published, and the duty to publish falls away.
#ASSERT     `s 57(a), (d) — the item is dealt with as the Law requires` `item (5) barred and not published` `where it is required:` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 57(a), (d) — the item is dealt with as the Law requires` `item (5) barred but published` `where it is required:` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 57(a), (d) — the item is dealt with as the Law requires` `item (5) barred but published` `where it is required:` FALSE
-- An item the Law does not require, left out or published, is no breach.
#ASSERT     `s 57(a), (d) — the item is dealt with as the Law requires` `item (6) not required, not published` `where it is required:` FALSE
#ASSERT     `s 57(a), (d) — the item is dealt with as the Law requires` `item (6) published` `where it is required:` FALSE

-- Whole publications.  An individual, no reduction: items (1), (2), (3) and (5).
#ASSERT     `s 57(a) — the publication deals with each item as the Law requires, given the items` (LIST `item (1) published`, `item (2) published`, `item (3) published`, `item (5) published`) `and the numbers required` (LIST 1, 2, 3, 5)
-- Item (3) is missing from the list altogether.
#ASSERT NOT `s 57(a) — the publication deals with each item as the Law requires, given the items` (LIST `item (1) published`, `item (2) published`, `item (5) published`) `and the numbers required` (LIST 1, 2, 3, 5)
-- Item (2) is listed but not published and not omitted under s.9(b).
#ASSERT NOT `s 57(a) — the publication deals with each item as the Law requires, given the items` (LIST `item (1) published`, `item (2) left out`, `item (3) published`, `item (5) published`) `and the numbers required` (LIST 1, 2, 3, 5)
-- Item (2) omitted as s.9(b) allows; item (5) barred by s.9(a) and not published.
#ASSERT     `s 57(a) — the publication deals with each item as the Law requires, given the items` (LIST `item (1) published`, `item (2) left out as s 9(b) allows`, `item (3) published`, `item (5) barred and not published`) `and the numbers required` (LIST 1, 2, 3, 5)
-- A corporation after a reduction needs all six.
#ASSERT     `s 57(a) — the publication deals with each item as the Law requires, given the items` (LIST `item (1) published`, `item (2) published`, `item (3) published`, `item (4) published`, `item (5) published`, `item (6) published`) `and the numbers required` (LIST 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6)
#ASSERT NOT `s 57(a) — the publication deals with each item as the Law requires, given the items` (LIST `item (1) published`, `item (2) published`, `item (3) published`, `item (5) published`, `item (6) published`) `and the numbers required` (LIST 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6)

-- The duty (a MUST, no time limit), guarded by the items and by the transparency of the publication.
#TRACE `s 57(a) — the Commissioner must publish the particulars of the financial sanction` TRUE FALSE `an individual` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `publish on the Ministry website the particulars of the financial sanction` `the Commissioner` (LIST `item (1) published`, `item (2) published`, `item (3) published`, `item (5) published`) TRUE AT 30
#TRACE `s 57(a) — the Commissioner must publish the particulars of the financial sanction` TRUE FALSE `an individual` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `publish on the Ministry website the particulars of the financial sanction` `the Commissioner` (LIST `item (1) published`, `item (2) published`, `item (3) published`, `item (5) published`) FALSE AT 30
#TRACE `s 57(a) — the Commissioner must publish the particulars of the financial sanction` FALSE FALSE `an individual` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 30)

-- (b): an appeal was filed: publish the filing, and its result once there is one.
#TRACE `s 57(b) — the Commissioner must publish the appeal and its result` TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `publish on the Ministry website that an appeal was filed and how it ended` `the Commissioner` TRUE FALSE AT 7
#TRACE `s 57(b) — the Commissioner must publish the appeal and its result` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `publish on the Ministry website that an appeal was filed and how it ended` `the Commissioner` TRUE FALSE AT 7
#TRACE `s 57(b) — the Commissioner must publish the appeal and its result` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `publish on the Ministry website that an appeal was filed and how it ended` `the Commissioner` TRUE TRUE AT 7
#TRACE `s 57(b) — the Commissioner must publish the appeal and its result` FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 7)

§§ `s 57(c): the name of an individual violator may be published, after a hearing, if necessary to warn the public`

-- individual, a separate opportunity, necessary, not barred: yes.
#ASSERT     `s 57(c) — the Commissioner may publish the name of the violator` `an individual` `who was given a separate opportunity:` TRUE `by the notice of intention` `a complete notice of intention delivered on 3 March 2027` `the Commissioner thinking publication necessary to warn the public:` TRUE `and the name being barred by section 9(a):` FALSE
-- no separate opportunity, but the notice of intention announced the intention (the s.43 right serving as the hearing): yes.
#ASSERT     `s 57(c) — the Commissioner may publish the name of the violator` `an individual` `who was given a separate opportunity:` FALSE `by the notice of intention` `a notice of intention that announces publication of the name` `the Commissioner thinking publication necessary to warn the public:` TRUE `and the name being barred by section 9(a):` FALSE
-- neither a separate opportunity nor an announcement: no.
#ASSERT NOT `s 57(c) — the Commissioner may publish the name of the violator` `an individual` `who was given a separate opportunity:` FALSE `by the notice of intention` `a complete notice of intention delivered on 3 March 2027` `the Commissioner thinking publication necessary to warn the public:` TRUE `and the name being barred by section 9(a):` FALSE
-- a corporation: (c) is about an individual; a corporation's name is item (6) already.
#ASSERT NOT `s 57(c) — the Commissioner may publish the name of the violator` `a corporation` `who was given a separate opportunity:` TRUE `by the notice of intention` `a complete notice of intention delivered on 3 March 2027` `the Commissioner thinking publication necessary to warn the public:` TRUE `and the name being barred by section 9(a):` FALSE
-- not thought necessary to warn the public: no.
#ASSERT NOT `s 57(c) — the Commissioner may publish the name of the violator` `an individual` `who was given a separate opportunity:` TRUE `by the notice of intention` `a complete notice of intention delivered on 3 March 2027` `the Commissioner thinking publication necessary to warn the public:` FALSE `and the name being barred by section 9(a):` FALSE
-- barred by s.9(a): no.
#ASSERT NOT `s 57(c) — the Commissioner may publish the name of the violator` `an individual` `who was given a separate opportunity:` TRUE `by the notice of intention` `a complete notice of intention delivered on 3 March 2027` `the Commissioner thinking publication necessary to warn the public:` TRUE `and the name being barred by section 9(a):` TRUE

#TRACE `s 57(c) — the Commissioner's power to publish an individual's name` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `publish the name of an individual violator on the Ministry website` `the Commissioner` AT 30
#TRACE `s 57(c) — the Commissioner's power to publish an individual's name` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 30)

§§ `s 57(d): a particular that s.9(a) of the Freedom of Information Law bars is not published`

#TRACE `s 57(d) — the Commissioner shall not publish a particular that section 9(a) bars` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `publish a particular on the Ministry website` `the Commissioner` `item (5) barred but published` AT 30
#TRACE `s 57(d) — the Commissioner shall not publish a particular that section 9(a) bars` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `publish a particular on the Ministry website` `the Commissioner` `item (5) published` AT 30

§§ `s 57(e): four years for a corporation, two for an individual (kind V, IL s.10(b), no s.10(c))`

#ASSERT `s 57(e) — the last day of the publication period that began on` (YMD 2027 9 1) `for` `a corporation` EQUALS YMD 2031 9 1
#ASSERT `s 57(e) — the last day of the publication period that began on` (YMD 2027 9 1) `for` `an individual` EQUALS YMD 2029 9 1
-- The month lacks the day: 29 February 2028 plus two years is 28 February 2030; plus four is 29 February 2032, which exists.
#ASSERT `s 57(e) — the last day of the publication period that began on` (YMD 2028 2 29) `for` `an individual` EQUALS YMD 2030 2 28
#ASSERT `s 57(e) — the last day of the publication period that began on` (YMD 2028 2 29) `for` `a corporation` EQUALS YMD 2032 2 29
-- Both edges of the period.
#ASSERT NOT `s 57(e) — the day` (YMD 2027 9 1) `is within the publication period that began on` (YMD 2027 9 1) `for` `an individual`
#ASSERT     `s 57(e) — the day` (YMD 2027 9 2) `is within the publication period that began on` (YMD 2027 9 1) `for` `an individual`
#ASSERT     `s 57(e) — the day` (YMD 2029 9 1) `is within the publication period that began on` (YMD 2027 9 1) `for` `an individual`
#ASSERT NOT `s 57(e) — the day` (YMD 2029 9 2) `is within the publication period that began on` (YMD 2027 9 1) `for` `an individual`
#ASSERT     `s 57(e) — the day` (YMD 2029 9 2) `is within the publication period that began on` (YMD 2027 9 1) `for` `a corporation`
#ASSERT     `s 57(e) — the day` (YMD 2031 9 1) `is within the publication period that began on` (YMD 2027 9 1) `for` `a corporation`
#ASSERT NOT `s 57(e) — the day` (YMD 2031 9 2) `is within the publication period that began on` (YMD 2027 9 1) `for` `a corporation`
-- The alternative (F-VALID): IL s.10(c) applied.  Published Friday 3 September 2027, an individual's two years end on
-- Monday 3 September 2029; if that day is a holiday the alternative moves the end to Tuesday 4 September 2029.
#ASSERT `s 57(e) — the last day of the publication period that began on` (YMD 2027 9 3) `for` `an individual` EQUALS YMD 2029 9 3
#ASSERT `s 57(e) — with s 10(c) applied, the last day of the publication period that began on` (YMD 2027 9 3) `for` `an individual` `with` `Monday 3 September 2029 as a holiday` EQUALS YMD 2029 9 4
#ASSERT `s 57(e) — with s 10(c) applied, the last day of the publication period that began on` (YMD 2027 9 3) `for` `a corporation` `with` `Monday 3 September 2029 as a holiday` EQUALS YMD 2031 9 3

-- The Ministry's duty when the period ends: the window opens the day after the last day (732 days after publication
-- on 1 September 2027 for an individual; 1,462 for a corporation) and has no closing edge.
#ASSERT (Day (YMD 2029 9 2)) MINUS (Day (YMD 2027 9 1)) EQUALS 732
#ASSERT (Day (YMD 2031 9 2)) MINUS (Day (YMD 2027 9 1)) EQUALS 1_462
#TRACE `s 57(e) — the Ministry must apply technological measures when the publication that began on` (YMD 2027 9 1) `for` `an individual` `ends, if accepted means exist:` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Ministry` DOES `apply technological measures against viewing the published particulars` `the Ministry` AT 732
#TRACE `s 57(e) — the Ministry must apply technological measures when the publication that began on` (YMD 2027 9 1) `for` `an individual` `ends, if accepted means exist:` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 1_000)
#TRACE `s 57(e) — the Ministry must apply technological measures when the publication that began on` (YMD 2027 9 1) `for` `an individual` `ends, if accepted means exist:` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 1_000)

§§ `s 57(f): the Minister may set further ways of publishing (a MAY with no precondition the section states)`

#TRACE `s 57(f) — the Minister may set further ways of publishing the particulars` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `set further ways of publishing the particulars` `the Minister` AT 10
#TRACE `s 57(f) — the Minister may set further ways of publishing the particulars` AT 0 WITH
